stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> CheckInventory: OrderCreated

    CheckInventory: CheckInventory (Task, retry x3 backoff x2)
    InventoryDecision: InventoryDecision (Choice)
    ProcessPayment: ProcessPayment (Task, retry x3 backoff x2)
    PaymentDecision: PaymentDecision (Choice)
    CheckFraud: CheckFraud (Task, retry x3 backoff x2)
    FraudDecision: FraudDecision (Choice)
    PublishOrderApproved: PublishOrderApproved (events:putEvents)
    EndOutOfStock: EndOutOfStock (Succeed)
    EndPaymentFailed: EndPaymentFailed (Succeed)
    EndFraudRejected: EndFraudRejected (Succeed)

    CheckInventory --> InventoryDecision

    InventoryDecision --> ProcessPayment: inventoryStatus == AVAILABLE
    InventoryDecision --> EndOutOfStock: default (OUT_OF_STOCK)

    ProcessPayment --> PaymentDecision

    PaymentDecision --> CheckFraud: paymentStatus == APPROVED
    PaymentDecision --> EndPaymentFailed: default (FAILED)

    CheckFraud --> FraudDecision

    FraudDecision --> PublishOrderApproved: fraudStatus == APPROVED
    FraudDecision --> EndFraudRejected: default (REJECTED)

    PublishOrderApproved --> [*]
    EndOutOfStock --> [*]
    EndPaymentFailed --> [*]
    EndFraudRejected --> [*]

    note right of EndOutOfStock
        InventoryFailed, PaymentFailed and FraudRejected are
        published by the respective Lambda itself before the
        state machine reaches its Succeed state; EventBridge
        rules route each to the notification queue.
    end note
